A British corporal at a NATO exercise in Tapa ignored orders to remove his phone's SIM card, and was then hacked and blackmailed over nude photographs, Eesti Ekspress reported .
A court martial heard the case this summer and the soldier was demoted, but it is still not known whether criminals or a foreign intelligence service hacked the phone.
Corporal Daniel Barton-Kennedy was briefed before deploying to Estonia to remove his phone's SIM card for the whole stay, was told again after arriving at Tapa for the Eastern Warrior exercise in January 2026, but ignored the order.
