Russia is stepping up its campaign of arson and sabotage across Europe, increasingly recruiting petty criminals through social media to carry out attacks that test the limits of Western tolerance and risk causing mass casualties, Estonian security experts warn.
Almost every day brings news of hybrid attacks in Europe. Russia, in particular, is constantly testing how far it can go before its actions can be classified as a direct military attack. One increasingly common form of such attacks is arson, as illustrated by the fire at Milrem Robotics' factory in Lasnam&auml;e. Rather than trained James Bond-style operatives, the perpetrators are often local petty criminals.
